<title>PHILIPPINES: Indonesia to get $66 mln-loan from Asian Dev Bank.</title>
<headline>Indonesia to get $66 mln-loan from Asian Dev Bank.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank said on Thursday it privided $66 million loan for Indonesia to improve its water supply.</p>
<p>The bank loan will provide 55 percent of the total project cost of $119.4 million.</p>
<p>It will be repayable over 25 years at an interest rate in accordance with the bank's pool-based variable lending system for U.S. dollar loans which is now at 6.82 percent.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8937</p>
</text>
